  "body": "## Problem\n\nPost-merge run 44591582241 at `56c5a35e4` (the merge of PR #2770) is red.\nOne step of 933 failed: `[915] ui suites: egui_app`.\n\nThe test binary stopped with a signal, not with a failed assert:\n\n```\nrunning 8 tests\ntest selecting_the_retired_imgui_shell_refuses_with_rc_2 ... ok\ntest ui_equals_form_refuses_like_the_space_form ... ok\ntest ui_flag_without_a_value_refuses_with_rc_2 ... ok\ntest a_headless_start_refuses_a_file_it_cannot_open_by_name ... ok\ntest a_headless_start_with_a_broken_model_fails_by_name ... ok\nerror: test failed, to rerun pass `-p camcraft-ui --test egui_app`\n... (signal: 11, SIGSEGV: invalid memory reference)\n```\n\nFive of the eight tests passed before the signal. The log does not name the test that ran at that time.\n\n## What is known\n\n- The run before it (44580083255 at `744c0847b`) was green on the same runner.\n- PR #2770 changed only the machine page of the UI and its tests. It did not change `crates/ui/tests/egui_app.rs`.\n- The fault can be intermittent. Run 44596948231 at `e048b103c` is pending and gives the next reading.\n- The `report` job of the run was skipped (#1611), thus the workflow opened no issue.\n\n## Priority\n\n`P2`: a gate on main is red. A crash of the application is `P1` by the table. Raise the label if the fault repeats or if it is in product code and not in the test harness.\n\n## Work\n\n1. Read the next post-merge run. If `ui suites: egui_app` is green there, record it here.\n2. Find the three tests that did not report, and run the binary many times on Linux to reproduce the signal.\n3. Find the cause. Fix it with a pinning test, or close this issue with the evidence if the next runs are green and the cause is outside our code.\n",
